[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2724245808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-2724245808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":2724245808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iYLEw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-14T10:17:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:14:21Z","body":"To be honest I'm not sure this is the right / best way to solve this.\r\n\r\nRounding errors are expected to be different on different platforms.\r\n\r\nTo elaborate:\r\n* The documentation is essentially asserting that you'd get the same result when running `doctool` on a different platform, which is NOT the case for floating point.\r\n* Changing the core code to bodge around this is kind of a case of the \"tail wagging the dog\", so to speak. It will slow down these functions, just to work around a bug / design flaw in the `doctool`.\r\n* Now there could be a case for doing this for numerical reasons in core, but that case should be made separately as the result of a real problem seen by users, as it has a cost.\r\n\r\nAs for some other ideas how to solve:\r\n* Have the doctool use a limited number of sig figs such that these rounding errors don't change the result.\r\n* Also could cap values close to 0 and 1 (or maybe all whole numbers) to the whole number if they are within a small margin.\r\n* Use a deterministic float emulation library.\r\n\r\nSee e.g. : https://gafferongames.com/post/floating_point_determinism/\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2724245808/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733239583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-2733239583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":2733239583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6i6e0f","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T13:30:47Z","updated_at":"2025-03-18T13:30:47Z","body":"> As for some other ideas how to solve:\r\n> * Have the doctool use a limited number of sig figs such that these rounding errors don't change the result.\r\n> * Also could cap values close to 0 and 1 (or maybe all whole numbers) to the whole number if they are within a small margin.\r\n\r\nYeah I agree that something like this may be a better approach.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733239583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2949503345","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-2949503345","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":2949503345,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vzdlx","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-06T14:48:49Z","updated_at":"2025-06-06T14:48:49Z","body":"Has the original issue of this PR been solved by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98750, or is it not related?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2949503345/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3054465151","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3054465151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3054465151,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62D3B_","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T23:41:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T23:43:27Z","body":"The doctool output in master is correct, but this bug still exists, so this PR should go through as a fix.\r\n\r\nThe rounding error affects other users of the core function, it's not purely a documentation problem.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3054465151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352408250","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3352408250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3352408250,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H0bC6","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T14:13:31Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:13:31Z","body":"> To be honest I'm not sure this is the right / best way to solve this.\r\n> \r\n> Rounding errors are expected to be different on different platforms.\r\n> \r\n> To elaborate:\r\n> \r\n>     * The documentation is essentially asserting that you'd get the same result when running `doctool` on a different platform, which is NOT the case for floating point.\r\n> \r\n>     * Changing the core code to bodge around this is kind of a case of the \"tail wagging the dog\", so to speak. It will slow down these functions, just to work around a bug / design flaw in the `doctool`.\r\n> \r\n>     * Now there could be a case for doing this for numerical reasons in core, but that case should be made separately as the result of a real problem seen by users, as it has a cost.\r\n> \r\n> \r\n> As for some other ideas how to solve:\r\n> \r\n>     * Have the doctool use a limited number of sig figs such that these rounding errors don't change the result.\r\n> \r\n>     * Also could cap values close to 0 and 1 (or maybe all whole numbers) to the whole number if they are within a small margin.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure though to say that's a doctool issue. Technically, the `Color` issue here is larger than just doctool. Color computation could be wrong because of that in a game. So concentrating to fix the issue \"for doctool\" seems a red herring.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352408250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352446927","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3352446927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3352446927,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H0kfP","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T14:21:34Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:21:34Z","body":"> I'm not sure though to say that's a doctool issue. Technically, the Color issue here is larger than just doctool. Color computation could be wrong because of that in a game. So concentrating to fix the issue \"for doctool\" seems a red herring.\r\n\r\nFloating point determinism is not trivial to do because of rounding modes, and afaik can be a problem to do in performant code in multicore environment. There's quite a bit of literature on it.\r\n\r\nSee https://gafferongames.com/post/floating_point_determinism/ .","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352446927/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352471219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3352471219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3352471219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H0qaz","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T14:26:01Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:26:01Z","body":"What I mean is that this is a simple fix for an issue which can be occurring also outside doctool. Returning HSL {0,0,0} when SRGB is {0,0,0} makes sense IMHO.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352471219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352571446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3352571446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3352571446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H1C42","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T14:48:18Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:48:18Z","body":"> I would instead edit [thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h) to add that check instead of in Color. Seems cleaner.\r\n\r\nDone.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352571446/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491629203","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3491629203","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3491629203,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QHgiT","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T14:46:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T14:49:32Z","body":"The actual value / imprecision is not the issue here. When used in logic, both will lead to the same results. That means we don't need to fix the logic, we need to fix our doc diffs problem.\r\n\r\nCapping the precision of the docs could be a good solution, but that would cap us at just 6 post-floating point digits of precision. Probably more than needed in most situations, but I think it's less than expected in some `double` situations. A solution might be to cap it at 5/6 for floats, and more for doubles, but I'm not sure we are capable of differentiating since it's all `double` in `Variant`.\r\n\r\nI've got another potential solution in mind: We should be able to provide an explicit default value instead of auto-generating it (via `ADD_PROPERTY_DEFAULT`). Since our float printing is deterministic, this should also fix the issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3491629203/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3503567326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#issuecomment-3503567326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104112","id":3503567326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q1DHe","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T16:37:33Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T16:37:33Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3503567326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]